The *rank* of $T$ is $"rank"(T) = dim(im T)$ and the *nullity* is $"null"(T) = dim(ker T)$: the dimensions of the image and the kernel. Since $ker T$ is a subspace of $V$ and $im T$ is a subspace of $W$,
$ dim (ker T) <= dim V, quad dim(im T) <= dim W. $
For $T: V -> W$, $V$ is called the domain of $T$ and $W$ the codomain of $T$. The image of a point $vb(x) in V$ under $T$ is the vector $vb(x') = T(vb(x)) in W$.
